# Environment template for Atlas / The Third Place.
# Copy to .env.local for local dev, and set the same three vars in the
# Vercel project settings for deploys. NEVER commit real values.

# n8n Cloud base URL — still REQUIRED after the Phase 2E read flip:
# all writes (status/payment/cancel/order intake/expenses) go through n8n.
VITE_N8N_BASE_URL=https://your-n8n-host.example.com

# Supabase read path (required since Phase 2E — reads come from Supabase).
# Use the anon PUBLIC key ONLY. NEVER the service_role / sb_secret key —
# those live exclusively inside n8n.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# ── Server-only secrets (Phase 2G-D staff write routes) ──────────────────────
# Read via process.env INSIDE server routes only. NEVER prefix these with
# VITE_ (VITE_ values are inlined into the client bundle). Set in .env.local
# for dev and in the hosting project's server env for deploys.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-server-only
STAFF_WRITE_SECRET=your-shared-staff-secret

# ── Phase 3A order-automation bridge (OPTIONAL — leave unset to disable) ─────
# BOTH must be set or the bridge is skipped and orders proceed normally.
# Phase 3C: even when set, ONLY server-resolved bot channels (instagram/
# messenger — none producible yet) dispatch; normal customer/staff orders
# never do. Unsetting both remains the global emergency dispatch-off switch.
# The URL must be a NEW automation-only n8n webhook (NO order insert nodes) —
# NEVER the old third-place-order-test intake webhook (it inserts an order).
# The secret signs a short-lived HS256 JWT (Authorization: Bearer) and must
# equal the passphrase of the n8n JWT credential used by the webhook's
# JWT Auth (runbook § Phase 3A).
#N8N_ORDER_AUTOMATION_WEBHOOK_URL=https://your-n8n-host.example.com/webhook/your-new-automation-only-path
#N8N_AUTOMATION_SECRET=your-long-random-automation-secret

# ── Payment-review notification (OPTIONAL — leave unset to disable) ──────────
# Its OWN n8n webhook for the payment.reviewed event, sent after staff approve
# or reject a slip so the bot can answer the customer in their chat thread.
# PILOT SCOPE: it deliberately REUSES N8N_AUTOMATION_SECRET above to sign the
# same short-lived HS256 JWT (subject "payment.reviewed"), so the n8n JWT
# credential is shared with the order bridge — one fewer secret to rotate while
# the pilot runs. Split it out if the two workflows ever need separate trust.
# BOTH this URL and N8N_AUTOMATION_SECRET must be set or the notification is
# skipped silently and the staff review is entirely unaffected. Delivery is
# best-effort and never retried — n8n MUST deduplicate on eventId.
# See docs/payment-proof-tuesday.md § payment.reviewed.
#N8N_PAYMENT_REVIEW_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ── Outbound customer messaging (server-only — NEVER prefix with VITE_) ──────
# Shared secret n8n will send as the x-chat-messaging-secret header on
# POST /api/automation/send-chat-message. Its OWN secret (not STAFF_WRITE_SECRET,
# not PAYMENT_PROOF_SECRET, not BOT_SESSION_SECRET) — messaging a customer is its
# own power and rotates on its own schedule. Unset → the endpoint refuses every
# request (fails closed).
#
# ALSO keys the one-way chat_ref stored in chat_message_dispatches, so rotating
# it changes future chat_ref values and older rows stop correlating with newer
# ones. Nothing joins on chat_ref (it is an operational aid), so rotation is safe
# — see api/_lib/chatMessaging.server.ts.
#
# ⚠️ THIS IS NOW A LIVE SEND PATH for channel "messenger" whenever
# META_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN below is also set. n8n is still not wired to the route,
# but anyone holding this secret can make the app message a real customer.
CHAT_MESSAGING_SECRET=your-long-random-chat-messaging-secret

# Meta PAGE access token for the real Messenger send (Graph API
# POST /<version>/me/messages). Server-only, read per call inside the provider,
# never logged and never stored. Requires the pages_messaging permission.
#
# Unset → the endpoint answers a safe needs_review ("auth") for every Messenger
# send, consumes NO eventId, and makes no Graph API call. Unsetting it is the
# emergency send-off switch.
#
# NOT an app secret and NOT the verify token — a third value with its own blast
# radius. A leaked Page token can message every person who has messaged the
# Page, so rotate it in the App Dashboard if it is ever exposed.
#
# Instagram is NOT implemented: channel "instagram" is refused before the claim
# and never reaches the network, whatever this value is.
#META_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN=your-meta-page-access-token

# ── Meta Messenger callback (server-only — NEVER prefix with VITE_) ──────────
# GET+POST /api/automation/meta-messenger-webhook — the ONE URL entered in the
# Meta app's Messenger webhook field. It replaces the n8n receiver, which minted
# a DIFFERENT public URL per HTTP method and so could not satisfy Meta's single
# callback field. Receive-only: no Page access token, no Graph API call, no
# customer reply. See docs/meta-messenger-webhook.md.

# The handshake token. Any long random string — you choose it here AND type the
# SAME value into Meta's "Verify token" field. Unset → every GET verification is
# refused with 403 (fails closed), so Meta cannot subscribe the callback.
#META_MESSENGER_VERIFY_TOKEN=your-long-random-verify-token

# The Meta app secret (App Dashboard → Settings → Basic → App Secret). Keys the
# HMAC-SHA256 body signature Meta sends as x-hub-signature-256. Unset → every
# POST is refused (fails closed); an unsigned POST is an anonymous POST and is
# never processed. NEVER log, print, or commit this value.
#META_APP_SECRET=your-meta-app-secret

# OPTIONAL forward target for SANITIZED event metadata (counts, categories,
# timestamps — never message text, PSIDs, Page IDs, or attachments). Unset →
# the endpoint still verifies and answers 200 and makes NO external request.
# Best-effort: 5 s timeout, no retry, and a failure never changes the 200 Meta
# receives. n8n MUST deduplicate on eventId (Meta retries the same body).
#N8N_MESSENGER_EVENTS_WEBHOOK_URL=https://your-n8n-host.example.com/webhook/your-messenger-events-path

# ── Phase 3D secure bot sessions (server-only — NEVER prefix with VITE_) ─────
# Required for /api/automation/bot-session, /api/menu-session/resolve and
# /api/order/submit-session. Until they are set those routes answer safe 500s
# and nothing else changes; normal customer/staff checkout is unaffected.

# Inbound authentication for the trusted simulated chat adapter, sent as the
# x-bot-secret header and compared with timingSafeEqual. DELIBERATELY NOT
# STAFF_WRITE_SECRET: that one lives in staff-device localStorage, so sharing
# it would let any staff device mint bot sessions and would tie its rotation
# to the dashboards.
BOT_SESSION_SECRET=your-long-random-bot-inbound-secret

# HMAC-SHA256 key for DETERMINISTIC secure-link token derivation. MUST be a
# different value from BOT_SESSION_SECRET (different purpose, different blast
# radius, different rotation cadence). Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# ⚠️ ROTATION: existing links keep working, but an idempotent RETRY of a
# session created under the old key can no longer reproduce its token and
# fails closed with SESSION_TOKEN_UNRECOVERABLE (never a dead link). Rotate
# only in a window of at least the 24 h session TTL.
# ⚠️ This key plus a database dump makes every LIVE token recomputable
# (request_id is a stored column). That is inherent to "same link on retry" —
# an encrypted-token design has the identical exposure — and is bounded by the
# 24 h TTL and single-use checkout. Server-only; never in n8n; never logged.
BOT_SESSION_TOKEN_SECRET=your-long-random-token-derivation-secret

# Origin used to build the secure link "<PUBLIC_SITE_URL>/m#<token>".
# Preview and Production have different origins — set it per environment.
# Not derived from the request Host header, which is attacker-controllable.
PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-production-domain.example.com

# ── Payment proofs (server-only — NEVER prefix any of these with VITE_) ──────
# Payment slips arrive in the Instagram/Messenger chat and are filed by n8n
# through POST /api/automation/payment-proof. There is NO customer upload page
# and no second payment link, so none of this is ever readable by a browser.

# Shared secret n8n sends as the x-proof-secret header on the trusted intake
# endpoint. Its OWN secret (not BOT_SESSION_SECRET, not STAFF_WRITE_SECRET) so
# proof intake and ordering-link minting rotate independently. Unset → the
# endpoint refuses every request (fails closed).
PAYMENT_PROOF_SECRET=your-long-random-payment-proof-intake-secret

# Private Supabase Storage bucket holding payment-slip images. Create it
# MANUALLY (Storage → New bucket, Public = OFF) before deploying — see
# docs/payment-proof-tuesday.md. Defaults to "payment-proofs" if unset; set it
# only to use a different bucket name. Staff previews use short-lived signed
# URLs generated server-side; no object is ever public.
#PAYMENT_PROOFS_BUCKET=payment-proofs

# Static payment QR image URL returned in the order-details payload so the bot
# can put it in the chat receipt. A PUBLIC image link, never a secret or an
# account credential, and never per-order. Unset → the payload carries null and
# n8n supplies its own QR.
#PAYMENT_QR_URL=https://your-cdn.example.com/payment-qr.png

# OPTIONAL public handles for the "Start New Order" return-to-chat action.
# These are PUBLIC values (not secrets) kept server-side so the mapping lives
# in one place. A HANDLE ONLY — never a full URL: the server validates it
# against ^[A-Za-z0-9._]{1,60}$ and interpolates it into a fixed template
# (https://m.me/<handle> or https://ig.me/m/<handle>), so a misconfiguration
# can never redirect customers off-site. Unset or malformed → the UI shows
# generic return-to-chat instructions instead of a broken button.
#MESSENGER_PAGE_HANDLE=yourpagehandle
#INSTAGRAM_HANDLE=your.instagram.handle
